  "question": {
    "text": "In Young&#39;s double slits experiment, the position of 5<sup>th</sup> bright fringe from the central maximum is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The distance between slits and screen is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and wavelength of used monochromatic light is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>600</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>. The separation between the slits is:",
